This patch updates the HD-Audio ALC880/260 code driver such
that all board-specific decisions are made in a single function,
which sets variables that all other code simply uses directly
without decision making.

This has the benefits of:

* Isolating board-specific code to a single location
* Simplifying the rest of the code
* Unifying the code for ALC880/ALC260, which was previously separate.

Signed-off-by: Stephen Warren <swarren@nvidia.com>
---

Future plans:

* Probably will update patch_alc880/patch_alc260 to point codec->spec at
pre-canned pre-initialized static data structures (one per ALC880_XXX
enum value) so that we avoid huge complex switch statements etc. in
patch_alcNNN in the future.

* Implement support for the ALC880 system I have with different
codec->jack connectivity, which drove all this parameterization.

